Native ARM64 crypto provenance
=============================

The portable implementations, ARM64 ChaCha20 assembly, public wrappers, alias
helpers, and upstream test/vector files derive from golang.org/x/crypto v0.55.0:

  https://github.com/golang/crypto/tree/v0.55.0/chacha20
  https://github.com/golang/crypto/tree/v0.55.0/chacha20poly1305
  https://github.com/golang/crypto/tree/v0.55.0/internal/poly1305
  https://github.com/golang/crypto/tree/v0.55.0/internal/alias

Their original copyright notices are retained. The repository-root LICENSE includes the upstream BSD 3-clause license
and ARM64 attribution for generated FOSS declarations.

Local adaptations:

* Imports point to these local packages and their alias helper.
* ChaCha20 keeps upstream ARM64 vector assembly. The buffered XOR in its Go
  wrapper uses crypto/subtle.XORBytes instead of a byte-at-a-time loop.
* Poly1305 sum_arm64.s is a new ARM64 translation of the saturated-limb
  algorithm in upstream sum_generic.go and sum_loong64.s. sum_arm64.go is
  adapted from sum_asm.go, with a full-block assembly entry point and a Go
  fallback for partial blocks. It has not received independent review.
* Build constraints retain a portable fallback on non-ARM64, purego and
  non-gc builds. The AEAD dispatch uses the generic wrapper with these local
  ChaCha20 and Poly1305 implementations.
* FIPS-only checks use crypto/fips140.Enforced on Go 1.26 and later. Older
  toolchains retain the behavior of this module's existing dependency.
* Differential, carry-state, concurrent-use, and fuzz tests were added locally.

This implementation includes no OpenSSL source, generated OpenSSL assembly,
OpenSSL calls, or CGO dependency. The separate 32-bit ARM implementation under
tsasm/arm has its own provenance and is unchanged by this addition.
